<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 1</h2>
<p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1 of 5</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 5th Grade (CEFR: A1.3)</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Local Farm Stand</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Need Two Papayas, Please.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Identify specific information in announcements or recordings. Interactive: Engage in simple discussions on lessons or current events.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can identify specific items and their prices from announcements in the market (e.g., "Two papayas for three dollars." "This papaya costs two dollars."). Can engage in simple discussions about items bought at the market (e.g., "I buy bananas."). Can respond to questions about prices and quantities in role-play scenarios (e.g., "How much is the banana?" "It is six bananas for one dollar.").</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h3>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by showing flashcards or realia of different fruits and vegetables (e.g., papaya, banana, mango, pineapple, tomato). The teacher holds up each item and says its name clearly. Students listen and repeat chorally. The teacher then asks "What fruit is this?" and students listen and respond with the name. This activates prior knowledge and introduces core vocabulary for listening.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary words like "papaya" and "banana," emphasizing the initial /p/ and /b/ sounds. The teacher also demonstrates segmenting words into syllables, for example, clapping for each syllable in "ba-na-na" (ba-na-na has three syllables), and "pa-pa-ya" (pa-pa-ya has three syllables). Students listen and mimic the clapping and pronunciation.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding by asking simple questions related to the vocabulary and pronunciation.
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is this a banana or a mango?" (Teacher points to a banana).</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How many sounds do you hear in 'papaya'?" (Clap the syllables as an example).</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Local Farm Stand")</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher plays a short audio recording (1-1.5 minutes) of a farm stand vendor announcing daily specials, prices, and availability of items. The audio includes phrases like: "Welcome to the farm stand! Today we have fresh papayas. Two papayas for three dollars. Bananas are cheap today, six bananas for one dollar. Do you need any mangoes? We have delicious mangoes for two dollars each. We also have some fresh eggs and milk. How much is this pineapple? It's four dollars. Can you help me, please? Thank you!"</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: Receptive: Identify specific information in announcements or recordings.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the recording about?" (e.g., A farm stand, shopping for food). Students listen and respond orally.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Matching:</b> Students receive a worksheet with pictures of items (papaya, banana, mango, egg, milk, pineapple) and prices listed randomly. They listen to the recording again and draw lines to match the item with its correct price or quantity mentioned.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students listen to specific statements about the recording (e.g., "The farm stand has oranges." "Two papayas cost three dollars.") and mark them as True or False on their worksheet. The teacher pauses the audio as needed for clarification.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> WH-questions ("How much is...?"), "Some" and "any", Polite requests ("Can you help me, please?").</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> mango, pineapple, papaya, banana, egg, milk, price, buy, sell, cost, cheap, fresh.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled practice / Cloze listening:</b> Students receive a printed transcript of the audio announcement with certain key words (e.g., prices, item names like "papayas," "bananas," "dollars") blanked out. The teacher plays the audio again, pausing at the blanks. Students listen carefully and write the missing words. The teacher then reviews answers by playing the audio once more and pausing to check specific words.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled substitution drill (Listening for availability):</b> The teacher reads aloud simple questions about item availability (e.g., "Do you have any apples?" "Do you have any pineapples?") using words not explicitly in the recording but from the vocabulary list. Students listen and respond chorally or individually with "Yes, we have some." or "No, we don't have any." based on what they remember from the recording or general knowledge (e.g., the recording didn't mention apples, but mentioned pineapples).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair interaction / Peer check (Listen and point/draw):</b> Students work in pairs. Each pair gets a "Farm Stand Menu" with pictures of various items (papaya, banana, mango, egg, cheese, bread, milk) and spaces for prices. One student (Customer) secretly "buys" 3-4 items and their quantities/prices (e.g., "I buy two papayas for three dollars."). The other student (Vendor) listens and draws/writes the bought items and their prices on their menu. They then switch roles. The focus is on active listening to identify specific items and prices.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">12-15 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Paired Role-Play: "Shopping at The Local Farm Stand."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in pairs. One student acts as the "Farm Stand Vendor" and the other as the "Customer." Each pair receives a set of item cards (with pictures and prices like "Papaya: $1.50 each", "Banana: 6 for $1", "Mango: $2 each", "Eggs: $3 per carton") for the vendor, and a "Shopping List" for the customer. The customer's shopping list asks them to buy 2-3 specific items (e.g., "need 2 papayas", "need some bananas"). The vendor starts by announcing some specials (e.g., "Welcome! Fresh papayas today!"), and the customer asks questions about items and prices, listening carefully to the vendor's responses. The customer must listen to the vendor's announcement and specific answers to complete their shopping list accurately by drawing or writing the items and total price. The vendor must listen to the customer's requests and respond appropriately. They use target language like "How much is...?", "Do you have any...?", "I need...", "Can you help me, please?".</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the role-play, focusing on listening comprehension and appropriate responses.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> During the role-play, the teacher circulates and uses a checklist to assess each student's ability to:
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Identify specific items and prices from verbal input (Customer).</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Respond appropriately to questions about availability and price (Vendor).</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear pronunciation of key vocabulary like "papaya", "banana", "price".</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Used at least 5-7 target words (e.g., papaya, banana, mango, price, buy, need, fresh, cheap).</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity of listening comprehension:</b> Correctly understood and responded to questions/statements about items and prices.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Engaged actively and respectfully with their partner.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short exit ticket with the following prompts:
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Name two items you heard today at the farm stand."</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Circle the correct price: Two papayas for (two / three) dollars."</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new words did you learn to listen for today?"</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Was it easy or difficult to understand the prices? Why?"</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students listen for specific information and respond? The audio announcement with clear prices and item names was effective. The matching activity helped students focus.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? Some students struggled with differentiating prices quickly. For the next lesson (Reading), I will provide written labels with pictures to reinforce vocabulary and link written words to prices visually. I will also incorporate more visuals during listening activities.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson introduced new vocabulary and concepts related to the farm stand through listening. In Lesson 2, students will encounter these same vocabulary words and phrases in a short written text, focusing on reading comprehension to reinforce their understanding and prepare them for more active language use.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>